  "extraction_notes": "All five data tables are on page 2 (single-column groundwater system; ranges are across wells). No violations section; the report states Gilroy's drinking water 'continues to meet all applicable drinking water quality requirements' and Table 1 shows 0 months in violation. Table 1 (coliform) gives counts ('1 (in a month)', '0 (in a year)') rather than percentages, so those entries carry count values with descriptive unit_raw. Lead/copper are from the 5/14/2024 triennial round; sodium, hardness, fluoride and the secondary rows are from a 2/14/2024 sample date; nitrate, PCE, TTHM, HAA5 are 2025 quarterly/monthly. 'ND' range lows are stored as 0. PHG (MCLG) column strings are copied verbatim (e.g. '1 (NA)'). Lead 90th percentile printed 0.00 is stored as value 0.0 with detected=false. Text verified against a rendered image of page 2."
